From 97006c3daa5f7d9af03b54f454ede48b6e45f478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:27:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tui remote caches: bystander replica rows keep no
 cards

On the mini the hub replica holds 18,635 task rows from 11 gateways, 87 MB of JSON. The serve retained a decoded
projection of every row: the sweep projection `_rows`, `_sweep_memo`, the observation flights (`_retained`),
`_memo` and `_known`. Together that was about 45 MB of the 890 MB replay footprint. Only a row linked to this
gateway can produce a card, a notice or an observation that it reads.

A row is held compact when all of the following are true: `hermes_cli.kanban_replica_relevance.is_bystander`
(imported, not copied) says it is a bystander; `_linked_chats(task, me)` is empty, which also covers
`withdrawal_recipients`; its seq is an int; its owner has no '/'; and it has a status. If in doubt (a duplicate
ref, a hash collision, a malformed row), the row keeps its full form.

- remote_sweep_projection: `_rows` is `{ref: "seq\0state" | (seq, cards, entry)}` and is mutated in place per
  scope. `states` is one live `StatesView` Mapping per scope. It is updated by the rows that changed, and is not
  rebuilt on every call. A compact row reads as `(state, CompactTask)`. A compact row whose legacy
  `<board>/<id>` twin appears is read again in the same snapshot. Payload SQL is unchanged and paged in one
  snapshot (#2409).
- `_settle_stale_claims`: for a compact row it reads the sessions back with a seq-checked point read
  (`CompactTask.load`). If the row moved, it waits one pass.
- observations: compact rows live in per-flight sorted `array('q')` columns of hash/seq/state-hash
  (kanban_remote_observation_compact). Their terminal states are still written to the ledger in the same
  transaction, under main's `first_seen` rule. They never enter decoded, Observed, `_memo` or `_known`.
  `_known` is pruned to the current cards' states. A second ledger path turns the lane off. A replaced ledger
  file triggers a re-read.

Proof: tests/tui_gateway/test_remote_projection_bystander_memory.py (5 tests).
- On main, all 5 are RED. (a) retains 1,275 bytes per bystander row. (c) gets main's settlement (profile from
  the read-back sessions) and fails only on its compact check.
- On this branch, all 5 are GREEN: below 300 B/row, and no bystander payload text is reachable from the five
  roots.
- 49 test files that import the changed modules (every tui_gateway remote/replica suite, including
  test_remote_index_projection_memory and test_replica_bounded_reads): 699 passed. No existing assertion was
  edited.
- `scripts/check --base origin/main` passes.
